<div class="row justify-content-center">
  <div class="col-md-8">
    <h1 class="mb-4">About This App</h1>

    <div class="card mb-4">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h4>Data Sources</h4>
        <p>This application uses data from the following three sources:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Open Library API</strong> —
            A free open API by the Internet Archive containing millions
            of books and authors. No API key required.
            Visit <a href="https://openlibrary.org/developers/api" target="_blank">openlibrary.org</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Custom CSV file</strong> —
            A curated list of book subjects and genres used to
            organize the collection into categories.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Faker Gem</strong> —
            Randomly generated book reviews to simulate
            real user-generated content.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h4>Database Schema</h4>
        <p>The app uses 5 tables:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Books</strong> — title, year, cover image, subject</li>
          <li><strong>Authors</strong> — name, bio, birth date</li>
          <li><strong>Subjects</strong> — name/category of books</li>
          <li><strong>Reviews</strong> — body, score, reviewer name</li>
          <li><strong>AuthorBooks</strong> — join table linking books and authors</li>
        </ul>
        <h5 class="mt-3">Associations</h5>
        <ul>
          <li>A subject has many books</li>
          <li>A book belongs to a subject</li>
          <li>Books and authors have a many-to-many relationship</li>
          <li>A book has many reviews</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>